  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_vrdant",
      "name": {
        "en": "Verdant's Badge",
        "zh": "维荻证章",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "uniequip_001_vrdant",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator Verdant has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude for repeated contention with the enemy upon the battlefield.\nThe Field Operations Department has thus passed the following resolution:\nThis operator shall be appointed a Specialist Operator during field operations to exercise Dollkeeper responsibilities.\nIn witness whereof,\nThis badge is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员维荻擅长于战场上同敌人反复周旋\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为特种干员，行使傀儡师职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_vrdant",
      "name": {
        "en": "Trophies from the Jungle",
        "zh": "密林撷萃",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "Y",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_vrdant",
      "description": {
        "en": "Verdant only manages a single step before a vine thicker than his arm bursts out from the bushes, lunging straight for his waist. The guide by his side tosses a spear, and as if conscious, the vine shrinks back into the tangle.\n'How do they grow so thick?!'\nThe guide scratches his head. 'That's just how they are. You're only here because you were after them, right? How could you not know?'\n'Suppose my boss was lying by omission then,' Verdant sighs. 'He said, there's carnivorous plants snapping about in the depths of the Acahuallan jungle. Keep one indoors, sorts out your Originium slug problem just like that. The big new thing amongst the Victorian gentry, he was betting...'\nThe guide only half-comprehends. All he can really think to ask is 'Do you still want one, then?'\nVerdant clutches his head in his hands. 'Just give me a bit to think about it. He'll be right storming if I don't get a sample, but I want to make sure I save my own <i>life</i> first.'\n'Huh? Save your life? Didn't you tell us you could take on five of our tribe's warriors before we left? Five of us could handle that thing no problem. You think the chief'd let me come here alone with you otherwise?'\n'Well... listen, just think of it as the terms of the job...'\nAt that moment, a vine silently ensnares the guide's ankle, and tugs him away for the undergrowth. Verdant hastily grabs hold of his hand, but the vine's stronger than he expects—so strong, he feels like his shoes are practically plowing the soil under him.\nHe curses his boss in his head, then with his free hand, switches out the vial on his saw, points at the guide's ankle and pulls the trigger. Out bursts a chemical spray, and in no time, the vine around his leg, and the entire thicket, have all withered yellow.\nThe guide springs back up from the ground. 'Brother, thank you! I don't know what to even say—we can pluck that thing and bring it back now!'\n'No, forget it. That was my strongest defoliant I just sprayed—the whole plant's on the way out. Not much point even picking it now.'\n'That's fine, there's always next time! With your wonder drugs, next time we'll get it for sure!'\n'Um, right.'\n'Let me tell you, people who can't back up their words are the kind our tribe hates most, and until just now, I thought you were sketchy as hell, but you did that thing in one go! Now I believe you—you CAN take five at once!'\n'W-Well, yeah, sure I can.'\n'I've got to tell the whole tribe when we get back how you're—you're this!' The guide throws Verdant a thumbs up. 'I bet people'll want to wrestle you, but you'll be fine! Just give 'em a puff of that drug and they'll soften right up, then even a little runt like you can flick 'em over, hahahaha!'\nUnprepared for the guide to start chattering away, Verdant blushes and quietly listens, picturing the proud Tiacauh coming to challenge him one after another. A helpless chill runs down his spine.\nBut compared to heading back and coping with his boss's thunderous temper... maybe this isn't so bad, he suddenly thinks.\nSo tonight he'll drop the pretense, eat and drink merrily, and prepare to get thrashed a couple dozen times.",
        "zh": "维荻刚朝前迈出一步，灌木丛中就突然伸出一根比手臂还粗的藤蔓，直奔他的腰间。一旁的向导甩出投矛，藤蔓像是有意识一样缩回了灌木丛中。\n“怎么会这么粗？！”\n向导搔了搔头：“就这么粗呀。你不就冲着它来的吗，咋可能不知道？”\n“出发前老板可不是这么说的，”维荻叹了口气，“在他嘴里，这是阿卡胡拉密林深处活泼好动的食虫植物，养一盆就可以一劳永逸摆脱室内源石虫困扰，必将成为维多利亚上流人士的新宠……”\n向导听得半懂不懂，只好问道：“那你还要不要？”\n维荻双手抱头：“我再想想吧，采不到样品老板肯定大发雷霆，可我总得先想想怎么把命保住。”\n“啊？保命？出发前你不是说我们部族的勇士你一个人能打五个吗？这玩意儿五个人肯定对付得过来，要不然酋长咋可能只让我一个人跟你过来？”\n“这……你就当这是一种工作需要……”\n一根藤蔓在此时悄悄缠上向导的脚踝，要把他拖进灌木丛里。维荻赶忙拉住向导的手，但藤蔓的力气大得出奇，维荻甚至能感受到自己的鞋钉正在像犁一样翻开脚下的土地。\n维荻在心里暗骂了老板一声，单手给手锯换上液罐，对着向导的脚踝扣动扳机。药雾喷出，很快，从向导脚上的藤蔓开始，整个灌木丛都变得一片枯黄。\n向导一骨碌从地上爬起来：“哥们，多亏了你！现在怎么说，可以把那玩意儿摘回来了吧！”\n“别想了，我刚喷的是最强效的落叶剂，现在整株植物都保不住，采回去也没用了。”\n“没关系，还有下回！有你的神药，下回肯定能行！”\n“唔，嗯。”\n“我跟你说，我们部族最讨厌说大话的人了，刚才看你那样子，我还以为你也是个不靠谱的，可你一下就把那玩意儿干掉了！你说你能打五个，我信！”\n“那、那当然了。”\n“回了部族我得告诉所有人，你是——这个！”向导对维荻竖起大拇指，“到时候可能有人来找你摔跤，你肯定没问题！你那神药冲着人一喷，人肯定也软了，你这样的小个子也能轻松撂倒，哈哈哈哈！”\n向导突然打开了话匣子，维荻红着脸听着，想到自称提亚卡乌的人们轮番来找自己挑战的样子，不由得感到一阵恶寒。\n但和回去应付暴跳如雷的老板相比……他突然觉得这样也不坏。\n今晚就放下伪装，大吃大喝，然后做好被摔在地上几十遍的准备吧。",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
